  "text": "### What We Built\nA comprehensive CLI for Plex Media Server management. Key commands:\n- `match search/apply` - Fix metadata matches (like Plex's \"Fix Match\" UI)\n- `editions` - List movies with editions, diagnose format issues with specific fix suggestions\n- `streams list/set` - Manage audio/subtitle tracks for entire seasons at once\n- `watch now/history/stats` - View activity, history, most watched by user/show/title\n- Added section column to `recently-added` and `file-paths` to identify duplicates across libraries\n\n### Technical Decisions\n- Module path: `github.com/dogbertdev/plexcli`\n- Uses published plexgo v0.27.0 SDK (had to fix many API compatibility issues - types changed to `any`, pointers everywhere)\n- Created `anyToString()` helper that properly dereferences pointers via reflection\n- Direct HTTP calls for auth (SDK removed Authentication API) and watch/streams features\n- XML parsing for Plex API responses (sessions, history, accounts, streams, matches)\n\n### Plex API Endpoints Discovered\n- `/status/sessions` - Active playback sessions\n- `/status/sessions/history/all` - Watch history\n- `/accounts` - User accounts\n- `/library/metadata/{id}/matches?manual=1` - Search for metadata matches\n- PUT `/library/metadata/{id}/match?guid=...` - Apply a match\n- PUT `/library/parts/{id}?audioStreamID=...&subtitleStreamID=...` - Set default streams\n- `/library/metadata/{id}/children` - Get seasons/episodes\n\n### Edition Tag Format\nPlex expects: `{edition-Name}` (lowercase, dash separator)\nCommon issues: `{Edition Name}` (capital E, space) - won't be recognized\n\n### CI/CD Setup\n- GitHub Actions for CI (Go 1.21/1.22 matrix, golangci-lint)\n- goreleaser for cross-platform builds (linux/darwin/windows, amd64/arm64)\n- Release workflow triggers on tags\n\n### Git History Cleanup\nUsed `git filter-repo --invert-paths --path plex --path cmd.test` to remove ~28MB of binaries from history before release.",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes",
    "plexcli - Production Release Session"
  ],
